    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0613" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/8–1750</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Webb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-08-17">August 17, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Meeting With The President, Thursday, August</hi>
                    17, 1950</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">bombing of rashin</hi>
                </p>
                <p>I showed the President a number of excerpts from Mr. Kennan’s reports of August 8
                    and 14<anchor n="1" xml:id="d439-f1"/> with respect to the present pattern of
                    Soviet intentions, and also the attached letter under date of August 16 to
                    Secretary Johnson, with respect to the Rashin bombing. The President’s first
                    reaction was that he thought we would have to take whatever risks were necessary
                    to destroy the points from which supplies were flowing, but when I made the
                    point that departures from agreed instructions should not be made without
                    thorough consultation with the State Department on the political implications,
                    the President agreed.</p>
                <p>I later had a brief conversation with Secretary Johnson on this matter and he
                    also agreed that we should have such prior consultation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
